  "termsDraftBody": "CUSTOMER TERMS AND CONDITIONS — DRAFT PREVIEW ONLY\n\nThis placeholder is not an approved legal agreement. It must be replaced with terms approved by the bank and Nigerian legal counsel before customer acceptance.\n\nService description: the product handoff describes a mobile banking app. The provider identity, regulated service description, foundation-bank relationship and applicable terms have not been supplied.\n\nEligibility and verification: the onboarding screens request identity details. Minimum age, eligibility criteria and account-opening conditions remain unconfirmed.\n\nTransactions, limits and fees: approved fee schedules, limits, settlement and reversal terms have not been supplied.\n\nSecurity and support: customers should protect authentication credentials. The approved support contact, complaint process and customer liability terms have not been supplied.\n\nBefore live use, legal owners must provide the effective date, document version, legal entity, fees, limits, complaint details, governing law, dispute terms and approval record.",
  "privacyDraftBody": "PRIVACY NOTICE — DRAFT PREVIEW ONLY\n\nThis placeholder is not an approved privacy notice. The controller, purposes and legal bases, recipients, retention periods, transfer locations, contact details and rights-handling process have not been approved.\n\nInformation entered: onboarding asks for phone number, name, date of birth, email, BVN and NIN. The app sends OTP requests and identity numbers to the API configured for the app. The responsible controller and processor details are not identified in the handoff.\n\nCamera and biometrics: the selfie step is intended for identity matching. The provider, processing location, retention/deletion schedule and failed-match process have not been supplied.\n\nPrivacy rights and contact: the applicable rights, request process, controller privacy contact and complaint route must be supplied by the privacy/compliance owner.\n\nBefore live use, obtain approved controller details, purposes and legal bases, recipient categories, transfer locations, retention and deletion rules, biometric-data details, rights process, effective date, version and approval record.",
